From f53312874b8124ea4f590f143a3ffdf6bdfef8b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:53:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/nvram: AT24CM02 2-Mbit I2C EEPROM, the EEPROM 3 Click

mchp-at24cm02 answers at four I2C addresses (A17:A16 in the address),
takes two word-address bytes, buffers page writes that wrap within the
256-byte page and commits them at STOP, then ignores its address for the
write cycle (ACK polling works). Its address counter survives between
transfers, so a current-address read after an address-only write reads
where the firmware pointed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
