diff --git a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
index 017a462..24c0655 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
@@ -175,6 +175,14 @@ headers, so one UART Click at a time; it then takes SERCOM3's place in
   ``connected``, ``central-tx`` (what it sends) and ``central-rx`` (what it
   received). CS (RTS) and INT (CTS) are not modelled.
 
+``eeprom3``
+  EEPROM 3 Click (v101a): an AT24CM02 2-Mbit EEPROM (``mchp-at24cm02``) at
+  I2C 0x50-0x53 (ADD jumper on 0; the address's low bits are A17:A16), WP
+  tied low. Two word-address bytes, page writes that wrap within 256 bytes,
+  the write cycle at STOP (``write-ms``, 5 ms, no ACK meanwhile), an address
+  counter kept between transfers, reads wrapping at 256 KiB. Erased at
+  power-up. ``view-at`` (hex) and ``view`` show 32 bytes for front ends.
+
 SPI Clicks on both headers share the SPI bus; each listens only while its
 own CS is low (or, for the 74HC595 and MAX7219, latches on its own CS).
 
